                "senderName": "NWS Miami FL",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued November 23 at 3:58PM EST until November 26 at 1:00AM EST by NWS Miami FL",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of southeast Florida, including the following\nareas, Coastal Broward County, Coastal Miami Dade County, Coastal\nPalm Beach County, Metro Broward County, Metro Palm Beach County\nand Metropolitan Miami Dade.\n\n* WHEN...From Tuesday evening through late Wednesday night.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nFlooding may occur in poor drainage and urban areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- The last 30 days of rainfall has been 400 to 600 percent of\nnormal across portions of Palm Beach and Broward Counties, and\nbetween 200 to 300 percent of normal across portions of\nMiami-Dade County. This amount of rainfall has made the ground\nvery saturated over the east coast metro areas of South Florida,\nand thus it will not take much rainfall to create exacerbated\nflooding issues across the east coast metro areas.\n\nMost likely amounts: 1-3 inches of rain Reasonable Worst Case\n(High-End): 4-6 inches of rain\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be alert for possible Flood\nWarnings. Those living in areas prone to flooding should be prepared\nto take action should flooding develop.",
                "response": "Prepare",
                "note": null,
