                "headline": "Flood Watch issued November 23 at 10:18AM PST until November 29 at 4:00PM PST by NWS Seattle WA",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of northwest Washington, including the following\ncounty, Mason.\n\n* WHEN...From Wednesday morning through Sunday afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- A series of storms will bring roughly 3 to 6 inches of rainfall\nto the southern slopes of the Olympics through Thursday with snow\nlevels rising to around 5000 to 5500 feet on Tuesday, and as high\nas 6000 to 6500 feet on Wednesday. The combination of heavy rain\nand relatively high snow levels is expected to push the Skokomish\nRiver near Potlach above flood stage by midweek.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be alert for possible Flood\nWarnings. Those living in areas prone to flooding should be prepared\nto take action should flooding develop.",
